# The three routes (/demo, /originate, /receive) are NOT here, and that is
# deliberate. Cloudflare Pages would not honour a 200 rewrite for them:
# rewriting to /index.html canonicalised straight to /, and rewriting to
# /app.html went to /app - both times throwing away the path that page.js
# reads to decide which route it is, which silently broke sharing a
# /receive link while looking fine locally.
#
# They are real directories instead, built from the one index.html at
# deploy time - see the "Assemble the upload" step in
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml, and spike/serve.py's RewritingHandler for
# the local equivalent.

